{"title": "Electrify Water", "pageid": 28426, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Electrify_Water", "categories": ["Passive item features", "Passive features"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-tooltip-box bg3wiki-tooltip-gradient-common\">\n<p><b>Electrify Water</b> is a passive feature that turns water surfaces into electrified water surfaces.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\"> Description </span></h2>\n<p>When the wearer stands in <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Water_(surface)\" title=\"Water (surface)\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/1c/Water_surface_Icon.webp/25px-Water_surface_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/1c/Water_surface_Icon.webp/38px-Water_surface_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/1c/Water_surface_Icon.webp/50px-Water_surface_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Water\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/1c/Water_surface_Icon.webp/25px-Water_surface_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/1/1c/Water_surface_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Water_(surface)\" title=\"Water (surface)\">Water</a> during combat, it becomes <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Electrified_Water\" title=\"Electrified Water\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/7/75/Electrified_Water_surface_Icon.webp/25px-Electrified_Water_surface_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/7/75/Electrified_Water_surface_Icon.webp/38px-Electrified_Water_surface_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/7/75/Electrified_Water_surface_Icon.webp/50px-Electrified_Water_surface_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Electrified Water\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/7/75/Electrified_Water_surface_Icon.webp/25px-Electrified_Water_surface_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/7/75/Electrified_Water_surface_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Electrified_Water\" title=\"Electrified Water\">Electrified Water</a>. \n</p>\n<div style=\"clear: both;\"></div>\n</div> \n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"How_to_learn\"> How to learn </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-tooltip-box\">\n<p>Granted by the equipment:</p><ul style=\"list-style: none;\">\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-block\" style=\"gap: 6px\"><span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-rare\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Watersparkers\" title=\"The Watersparkers\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/10/The_Watersparkers_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-The_Watersparkers_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/10/The_Watersparkers_Unfaded_Icon.png/45px-The_Watersparkers_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/10/The_Watersparkers_Unfaded_Icon.png/60px-The_Watersparkers_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/10/The_Watersparkers_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-The_Watersparkers_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/1/10/The_Watersparkers_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/The_Watersparkers\" title=\"The Watersparkers\">The Watersparkers</a></span></li>\n</ul>\n</div> <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\"> Notes </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-tooltip-box bg3wiki-tooltip\">\n<ul><li><b>Electrify Water</b> electrifys a surface of water immediately when entering it during combat, or when standing on one as combat starts. However, it will run out in a few turns and only reactivate by leaving and entering the area of the water again.</li>\n<li>Using this in combat where friendly but non-controllable NPCs are present may result in them turning hostile afterwards if they walk through electrified water surfaces.</li></ul>\n</div>   \n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714213707\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [no‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1359/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 11249/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 4079/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 25/200\nExpensive parser function count: 0/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 40/1000\nLua time usage: 0.009/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 817866/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   41.162      1 Template:Passive_feature_page\n100.00%   41.162      1 -total\n 42.17%   17.358      2 Template:Area\n 26.08%   10.734      2 Template:Area_inline/format\n 25.06%   10.314      2 Template:Icon_link\n 24.08%    9.910      2 Template:Icon_text\n 22.74%    9.360      1 Template:Passive_equipment_list\n 22.63%    9.313     10 Template:Trim\n 18.73%    7.711      4 Template:Ifempty\n 17.95%    7.387      1 Template:Passive_sources/format\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key bg3wiki:pcache:idhash:28426-0!canonical and timestamp 20260714213707 and revision id 370161. Rendering was triggered because: unknown\n -->\n</div>"}